WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.032
Choose one misconception from a unit you teach.

2
00:00:03.232 --> 00:00:08.636
Our example is the assumption that more sunlight must always be better for every plant.

3
00:00:08.836 --> 00:00:12.540
Select observations that make the decision less automatic.

4
00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:18.227
Create a model panel that names the claim, two pieces of evidence and a limitation.

5
00:00:18.427 --> 00:00:23.748
A clear small task is better than a board that tries to teach an entire unit at once.

6
00:00:23.948 --> 00:00:27.456
Build the partly completed example beside the model.

7
00:00:27.656 --> 00:00:32.147
Remove a reasoning step and leave a question that invites explanation.

8
00:00:32.347 --> 00:00:35.997
Create an independent case with different observations.

9
00:00:36.197 --> 00:00:39.802
Add one purposeful asset and its text equivalent.

10
00:00:40.002 --> 00:00:47.268
Decide how learners will respond by drawing, writing or speaking, using the same content criteria across response

11
00:00:47.468 --> 00:00:48.359
modes.

12
00:00:48.559 --> 00:00:51.007
Rehearse your think-aloud in about a minute.

13
00:00:51.207 --> 00:00:55.357
Ask a colleague to find the claim and evidence without your help.

14
00:00:55.557 --> 00:00:59.522
Check whether the role rotation gives each learner a chance to reason.

15
00:00:59.722 --> 00:01:02.144
Save and reopen the editable board.

16
00:01:02.344 --> 00:01:08.593
Your practice deliverable is the three-panel sequence, one visual asset and a short modeling script.

17
00:01:08.793 --> 00:01:14.023
Revise the instructions if a colleague cannot tell what students are meant to learn.

